# Comm Broadcast — {{ project_name }}

Post QA lifecycle notifications to **{{ comm_platform_label }}** channel
`{{ comm_platform_channel }}`. Notify-only — {{ comm_platform_label }} is never a
reconstruction source for pipeline state.

## When to use

| Trigger | Message type |
|---|---|
| Simple feature path complete | QA brief |
| All phases complete (done) | Deploy advisory |
| Rewrite ceiling hit (3 times) | Human escalation |
| Environment / blocker discovered | Blocker ping |

## Message Shapes

### 1. QA Brief (simple feature path)

Use when test-design-agent completes a `done_simple` ticket.

```
📋 *QA Brief — <ticket-key>* | {{ project_name }}

<Feature Name>

Scope: <what was tested>
Result: ✅ Passed | ⚠️ Conditional | ❌ Failed

Notes:
• <bullet 1>
• <bullet 2>

Ticket: <link>
```

### 2. Deploy Advisory (pipeline complete)

Use when automation-agent completes and all phases have passed.

```
🚀 *QA Advisory — <ticket-key>* | {{ project_name }}

*<Feature Name>* is ready for deploy review.

Coverage:
• {{ test_repo_label if has_test_repo else "Cases" }}: N cases
• Automated: N / N automatable
• Excluded: N (with reasons)

Compliance: ✅ PASS (0 critical, 0 major)

Ticket: <link>
{% if has_test_repo %}Test Run: <link>{% endif %}

⚠️ Do not merge until a human reviews the draft PR.
```

### 3. Human Escalation

Use when the 3-rewrite ceiling is hit for any phase.

```
🚨 *QA Escalation — <ticket-key>* | {{ project_name }}

Phase *<phase name>* has been rewritten 3 times without resolving violations.
Human review required before the pipeline can advance.

Last violation summary:
<paste the critical findings from convention-check>

Last actions taken:
<paste the actions_taken list from the last handoff contract>

Ticket: <link>
```

### 4. Blocker Ping

Use when a blocker is discovered (stale auth, missing AC, environment down).

```
⚠️ *QA Blocker — <ticket-key>* | {{ project_name }}

Blocker: <one-line description>
Impact: Pipeline halted at phase <name>
Action needed: <what a human needs to do>

Ticket: <link>
```

## Hard Rules

- Post to `{{ comm_platform_channel }}` only — never to DMs or other channels.
- **Never** include credentials, session tokens, or sensitive data in any message.
- **Never** use {{ comm_platform_label }} to reconstruct pipeline state — read `.claude/references/` instead.
- Keep messages concise — link to the full artifacts rather than pasting their content.
- One message per event — do not flood the channel with intermediate updates.
